# Allowlist, not a denylist. The build context is everything the images need
# and nothing else, so a build from a working checkout cannot copy stray local
# files into an image (and from there into any registry it is pushed to).
# Add a new "!path" line when the application genuinely needs a new file.
*

!enferno
!migrations
!flask
!tests
!run.py
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!pytest.ini
!uwsgi.ini
!reload.ini
!config.sample.json
!LICENSE

# Re-exclude generated and runtime data living inside the paths above.
# `tests/` is required by flask/Dockerfile.test, so it stays included.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[co]
**/node_modules
**/.DS_Store
enferno/media
enferno/imports
